# textures_gap_serializer_v2: Serializer textures (type 8) with v2 descriptors where only v1 ones were, each made by its first use in a copy with only the buffers listed (listing a serializer texture itself faults its prepare): a 2D array of two slices over a shared buffer through commandType 55 takes newLinearTextureWithDescriptor and its second slice copies out the buffer's bytes at +0x280 (slices 0x80 apart); 55 over an unknown buffer reference and 56 in an unknown heap fail ("Failed to get base buffer" / "base heap") and fault their copies. A normal texture (type 2, commandType 52) whose swizzle names channels 6, 7 and 0xff reads each as One, and is made when listed (shader-read only: Metal asserts on a swizzled texture that may be written).
